02Problem Statement
Problem Addressed
Students revising for exams or mastering unfamiliar subjects often rely on passive reading or isolated, single-turn AI queries. Single-turn interactions forget what the learner has already answered, fail to track which questions were missed earlier in the study session, and leave the student without a structured record of scores, weak subtopics, and targeted follow-up revision priorities once studying concludes.

Who Benefits
Students & Self-Learners: Gain an interactive personal tutor that asks one focused question per turn, evaluates responses fairly, awards marks (1 for correct, 0 for incorrect), revisits missed questions during revision, and produces an actionable end-of-session performance report.
Peer Study Groups & Educators: Can reopen dated JSON session archives directly from the main menu to review full conversation transcripts, question-by-question scores, and recommended areas for further study.
03Tool Description
During the Conversation
Menu-Driven Entry (main.py): Launching python main.py presents a three-option terminal interface: 1. New Study Session, 2. Open Past Session, and 3. Exit.
Session Initialization (main.py, memory.py, progress_tracker.py): When starting a new session, the student enters their name and study topic. The system validates non-empty inputs, initializes a conversation history list (initialize_memory), and creates an empty performance dictionary (initialize_progress).
Multi-Turn Memory & Question Loop (study_buddy.py): On every turn, the entire messages list is converted into Gemini conversation turns and transmitted to the model so every reply accounts for earlier questions, student answers, and feedback. The tool asks one question at a time, displays feedback and the next question, updates the live score and accuracy percentage, and conducts a revision pass on missed questions (get_revision_questions) when wrapping up.
Echo Intelligent Solutions — AI Study Buddy Project Report
Page 1 of 15
JSON Validation & Single Retry (json_validator.py): Every AI reply is parsed as JSON and verified against six required fields (status, question, feedback, is_correct, score, topics_to_revise). If validation fails, validate_with_retry automatically executes one retry before alerting the student and rolling back the unvalidated turn.
At the End of the Session
When the student enters end, exit, or finish, the assistant conducts revision attempts for any previously missed questions, builds a final summary request (prepare_summary_request in summary.py) combining the full conversation transcript and Python's authoritative progress records, validates the 11-field summary JSON (parse_summary_response), displays the formatted report (display_summary), and persists the session and summary to a dated JSON file in samples/ via session_manager.py (<Student_Name>_YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS.json). Saved sessions can be reopened anytime via option 2. Open Past Session.

04AI Instruction Design (R-T-C-C-O Framework)
Both prompts are defined in prompts.py and explicitly implement all five components of the R-T-C-C-O framework: Role, Task, Context, Constraints, and Output Format.

