05Technical Overview
Modular Architecture
Module	Primary Responsibility
main.py	Displays the 3-option CLI menu, validates non-empty student name and study topic inputs, and coordinates new sessions and past session viewing.
prompts.py	Stores SYSTEM_PROMPT and SUMMARY_PROMPT structured with the R-T-C-C-O framework.
memory.py	Initializes the conversation history list (initialize_memory) and appends user and assistant turns (add_user_message, add_ai_message).
study_buddy.py	Loads GEMINI_API_KEY via python-dotenv, converts full message history into Gemini turns (call_gemini), manages the quiz loop, records progress, and runs revision checks.
json_validator.py	Parses JSON responses, validates all 6 required fields and Python types (validate_ai_response), and executes one automatic retry on failure (validate_with_retry).
progress_tracker.py	Tracks total questions, correct/incorrect counts, score (1 or 0), accuracy percentage, and questions_to_revise.
summary.py	Builds the summary payload from the transcript and authoritative Python progress records (prepare_summary_request), validates the 11-field summary JSON (parse_summary_response), and renders the final report (display_summary).
session_manager.py	Saves completed conversations and summaries into dated JSON files in samples/ (save_session) and lists/loads saved archives (open_past_session).
How Memory, API Calls & Validation Work Together
In study_buddy.py, call_gemini() iterates through the complete messages list maintained by memory.py, translating "user" and "assistant" entries into Gemini's user and model turn format and passing the full history to client.models.generate_content(...) with response_mime_type="application/json". Every response is checked by validate_with_retry() in json_validator.py; if JSON decoding or schema validation fails, one corrective retry call is executed before rolling back the turn with messages.pop().

def validate_with_retry(response, retry_function):
    is_valid, result = validate_ai_response(response)
    if is_valid:
        return result

    print("\nInvalid AI response detected.")
    print("Attempting to generate a corrected response...")
    try:
        new_response = retry_function()
        is_valid, result = validate_ai_response(new_response)
        if is_valid:
            print("AI response successfully corrected.")
            return result
        print("The second response also failed validation.")
    except Exception as error:
        print(f"Retry failed: {error}")
    return None
